concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-1-sec-14-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14(2) Subdivision B of Division 4 of Part IIIAA"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-14-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The AER may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, make an arrangement with the appropriate authority or officer of: (a) a State or Territory government; or (b) a State or Territory government authority; under which the government or authority makes officers or employees available to the AER to perform services in connection with the performance of any of the AER’s functions." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The AER may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, make an arrangement with the appropriate authority or officer of: (a) a State or Territory government; or (b) a State or Territory government authority; under which the government or authority makes officers or employees available to the AER to perform services in connection with the performance of any of the AER’s functions."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "884b62be65f320b34ed3b07f19b7d6a263f195c84d5fd5b304785e54cba62dbb" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-1-sec-14 ;
    cof:pageNumber "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Government or authority makes officers or employees available to AER for services. Establishes a Statutory Agency with the AER Chair as its Head. Terms and conditions of engagement are determined by the AER." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
