concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1 Definitions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) In this Schedule: ACCC Enterprise Agreement means the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission Enterprise Agreement 2024-2027 approved under the Fair Work Act 2009 on 28 March 2024, as in force immediately before the commencement day. amending Act means the Competition and Consumer Amendment (Australian Energy Regulator Separation) Act 2025. commencement day means 1 July 2026. (2) Expressions used in this Schedule that are defined for the purposes of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 have the same meaning as in that Act.  Application, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2 Application, saving and transitional provisions  Part 2 No. 59, 2025 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Australian Energy Regulator Separation) Act 2025" ;
    skos:definition "(1) In this Schedule: ACCC Enterprise Agreement means the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission Enterprise Agreement 2024-2027 approved under the Fair Work Act 2009 on 28 March 2024, as in force immediately before the commencement day. amending Act means the Competition and Consumer Amendment (Australian Energy Regulator Separation) Act 2025. commencement day means 1 July 2026. (2) Expressions used in this Schedule that are defined for the purposes of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 have the same meaning as in that Act.  Application, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2 Application, saving and transitional provisions  Part 2 No. 59, 2025 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Australian Energy Regulator Separation) Act 2025"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "47f808859adb750df5f43c745735fb11d8f4b9abfd9aec20edac015a9f7b7031" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definitions for Schedule 2" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025.pdf, p.14" ;
    cml:asserts concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-1-norm .
concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-1-norm a values:Undertaking ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-1 ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "1 Definitions" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) In this Schedule: ACCC Enterprise Agreement means the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission Enterprise Agreement 2024-2027 approved under the Fair Work Act 2009 on 28 March 2024, as in force immediately before the commencement day. amending Act means the Competition and Consumer Amendment (Australian Energy Regulator Separation) Act 2025. commencement day means 1 July 2026. (2) Expressions used in this Schedule that are defined for the purposes of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 have the same meaning as in that Act.  Application, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2 Application, saving and transitional provisions  Part 2 No. 59, 2025 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Australian Energy Regulator Separation) Act 2025" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2 Delegations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This item applies in relation to a delegation if: (a) the delegation was made under section 44AAH of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 before the commencement day; and (b) the delegation is in force immediately before the commencement day. (2) The delegation continues in force (and may be dealt with), on and after the commencement day, as if it were a delegation made under section 44AAH of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010, as amended by the amending Act." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This item applies in relation to a delegation if: (a) the delegation was made under section 44AAH of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 before the commencement day; and (b) the delegation is in force immediately before the commencement day. (2) The delegation continues in force (and may be dealt with), on and after the commencement day, as if it were a delegation made under section 44AAH of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010, as amended by the amending Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "48f185621db5204aa434188f5502ebf04b2c964302b0a24202018f0d67ec8575" ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Delegation continues in force after commencement day." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025.pdf> ;
